The input thread reads ahead until it holds 96000 samples, 2.2 s at
44.1 kHz. Everything in that buffer is audio the phone has already
counted as played: a seek or a pause made there reaches the speakers
only once the buffer drains, on top of the 2 s the AirPlay receivers
hold. The buffer is not what keeps playback steady: the player streams
silence through a read deficit of up to 1.5 s (PLAYER_READ_BEHIND_MAX)
before it suspends, the pipe itself holds 64 KB, and the writer is a
local process blocked on the pipe, never behind. A quarter second is
slack for the 10 ms read loop and nothing more.

